{{also|dach|đách}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|dah|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*þaką}}; compare Low German {{term|Dack|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|dak|lang=nl}}, English {{term|thack|lang=en}}, {{term|thatch|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|tag|lang=da}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*teg-}}, and akin to Latin {{term|toga||garment|lang=la}} and Ancient Greek {{term|στέγος||roof|lang=grc}}.

